{
  "slug": "drift-detect",
  "name": "Drift Detect",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Deep repository analysis to realign project plans with actual code reality. `/drift-detect` discovers drift between documented plans (CHANGELOG, ARCHITECTURE.md, design docs, README claims) and what the code actually does, then produces a prioritized reconstruction plan. Pure JavaScript collectors gather data fast (no LLM overhead) and a single Opus call performs the deep semantic analysis - 77% fewer tokens than multi-agent approaches. Tested on 1,000+ repositories. Outputs a ranked list of drift items with severity, evidence, and suggested resolution.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, **1 agent** and **1 command**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `drift-analysis` (Use when the user asks about plan drift, reality check, comparing docs to code, project state analysis, roadmap…)\n- **Agents** (1): `plan-synthesizer` (Perform deep semantic analysis on collected project data to identify drift, gaps, and create a prioritized reconstruction plan)\n- **Commands** (1): `drift-detect` (Deep repository analysis to realign project plans with actual code reality)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install drift-detect@claude-community` from `agent-sh/drift-detect`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 1,
    "agent": 1,
    "command": 1
  },
